{"id": "EUVD-2026-108887", "enisaUuid": "845bedda-dad0-33c3-8acc-cb385732fe60", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: io: Reject non-user protection in ioremap_prot()\n\nMapping a stack-top page via /dev/mem with PROT_NONE and then\nreading that process's /proc/<pid>/cmdline triggers a spurious WARN\nin ioremap_prot() through generic_access_phys():\n\n  WARNING: ./arch/arm64/include/asm/io.h:275 at generic_access_phys\n  Call trace:\n    generic_access_phys+0x1c8/0x228 (P)\n    __access_remote_vm+0x2b4/0x398\n    access_remote_vm+0x14/0x30\n    get_mm_cmdline+0xf8/0x2a0\n    proc_pid_cmdline_read+0x68/0x120\n\ngeneric_access_phys() passes the protection derived from the user PTE\nto ioremap_prot(). On arm64, a PROT_NONE mapping is represented by a\npresent-invalid PTE, so pte_present() still returns true and the\nprotection reaches ioremap_prot().\n\nA PROT_NONE mapping does not have PTE_USER, causing the existing\nWARN_ON_ONCE() in ioremap_prot() to fire even though this is a valid\nuser mapping. Execute-only mappings have the same issue and must not\nbe readable through this path either.\n\nioremap_prot() should therefore reject protection values without\nPTE_USER without warning. This makes the access fail cleanly for\nPROT_NONE and execute-only mappings while retaining the existing\nuser-protection contract.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:03:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:05:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fddc90d4af4550af410f52d11bbf6b5f36443838", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b04af3d88bb7fc69b2d92457890608860e42365", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b17aa4955e3a694c663ebe99626e4c76ca4f7cfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b583795feb51f8d50203228d001760d1344ef01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb756b11ad63832ebee58caf9e8f9381eaecff9f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98923"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09d35b05-81ff-3331-9c4b-7f9e116b65b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64858b76ec67c5fc40fef8ec1841fecb78c1ebde <fddc90d4af4550af410f52d11bbf6b5f36443838"}, {"id": "0e3c8a1a-304b-3dcd-9f6f-bdb989d9405b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.93 <6.12.112"}, {"id": "17689b77-097e-3dfb-bcce-6fe6319cab41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2cea9e21-f578-34e7-910f-db1e785bb3ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1ad8fe7f72d73e1617bac79f2ec7a3bedf47e2a"}, {"id": "3e77544e-9444-3f01-8133-6b54ee259eaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3d64dcc0799c2d6921ba027716b7be721eb19fa8 <b17aa4955e3a694c663ebe99626e4c76ca4f7cfb"}, {"id": "4d346431-1f82-3441-b2fe-fd38ca21f41f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19.7 <6.20"}, {"id": "4e41f933-905b-3422-a458-3baa6aea69a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "619a76ca-06ad-32ee-bc73-9239b3cc06c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.143 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "697c4833-8377-3cae-abb0-4f940cce1d9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "72896873-509d-3890-aab2-9760744dad69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "7973e2e2-db48-3efd-b453-5e6a42037fbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "a037e606-f798-34c1-8f0c-df5e7b120402", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eeecafce5afffb4da703666ebefbd4d6e2a5abf6 <0b04af3d88bb7fc69b2d92457890608860e42365"}, {"id": "acd31fc7-3301-3cbe-a580-7c792a03598e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f098037139b294050053123ab2bc0f819d08932 <bb756b11ad63832ebee58caf9e8f9381eaecff9f"}, {"id": "cacc5c56-7ac7-3744-9be0-24a4f0cee579", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.17 <6.18.55"}, {"id": "d456f947-86b3-3080-88a2-5edfd977f3e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "e6d03772-0272-3ce8-b6ed-f3a2c83dcb9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8f098037139b294050053123ab2bc0f819d08932 <9b583795feb51f8d50203228d001760d1344ef01"}, {"id": "f5c85160-a45c-34df-95cc-8e2f549c2241", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c2345221-b892-3d3b-8591-7845f357b7b0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}